            <ArticleTitle>Neurofibromatosis type 1 and type I Chiari malformation: an unusual association.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>336-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report an 11-year-old boy with neurofibromatosis type 1 (NF1) and asymptomatic type I Chiari malformation. This association may be considered a pure coincidence, due to the relative frequency of the two conditions, but recent reports describing the same association suggest that type I Chiari malformation probably should be added to the list of abnormalities of the central nervous system reported in patients affected by NF1.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
